{"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Four ways a spell becomes available, over one way of writing what it does.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting","doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/init(memorySlots:maxMana:text:)","doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/memorySlots","doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/maxMana"],"anchor":"The-bundle","title":"The bundle"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/Text","doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/SpellList","doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/Energy"],"anchor":"The-systems-voice","title":"The system’s voice"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/spell(_:called:cost:effect:)"],"anchor":"Registering-a-spell","title":"Registering a spell"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost","doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost\/cantrip","doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost\/prepared(book:learnVia:)","doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost\/energy(_:)","doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost\/scroll(_:)"],"anchor":"The-four-paradigms","title":"The four paradigms"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/verbs","doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/actions","doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/noiseWords"],"anchor":"What-the-bundle-contributes-to-the-host","title":"What the bundle contributes to the host"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Gnusto"],"generated":true,"title":"Extended Modules","anchor":"Extended-Modules"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","title":"GnustoSpellcasting","modules":[{"name":"GnustoSpellcasting"}],"role":"collection","symbolKind":"module","externalID":"GnustoSpellcasting"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Magic systems differ in their bookkeeping, not in their effects. An at-will","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cantrip, a spell memorized from a book and spent in the speaking, a bolt paid","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for out of an energy pool, and a scroll good for one reading all do the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sort of thing to the world; what separates them is when the game says no. This","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"library keeps the two apart. A spell’s effect is an ordinary rule body, written","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exactly as any other rule body is, and a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" sits beside it deciding","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"availability and price.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A spell’s identity is its own intent, declared with ","type":"text"},{"code":"#verb","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" like any custom","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"verb, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"glow","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"cast glow","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"read passwall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are parser rows and a spell can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"carry as many phrasings as its author wants. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/spell(_:called:cost:effect:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"returns the actions that intent needs — the cast handler, plus the memorize","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"handler when the cost is ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost\/prepared(book:learnVia:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" — and the game","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"splices them into its ","type":"text"},{"code":"actions","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The layer’s own lines name a spell by its ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"word"}]},{"text":" — “You fix the unbar spell in your memory” — which is the intent’s name unless ","type":"text"},{"code":"called:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" says otherwise. An intent that is not a word a player reads, ","type":"text"},{"code":"#verb(\"castFire\", …)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", wants ","type":"text"},{"code":"called: \"fire\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or every line about it says “the castFire spell”. The word is display and nothing more: memory is keyed on the intent, so two spells may share a word and are still memorized, cast and spent one at a time.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"GameContent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" bundle rather than a ","type":"text"},{"code":"GamePlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", because it has state to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"save. The finite spell memory and the energy pool are ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Global","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s it owns, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"both travel in a save and come back correctly under UNDO; the defaults are 3","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"slots and 12 mana. Everything else is the host’s: the spellbook, the scroll, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"targets, and every word of prose an effect prints. The bundle contributes one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"verb of its own — ","type":"text"},{"code":"spells","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (or ","type":"text"},{"code":"magic","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), which reports what is held in mind and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"how much energy is left — promotes the engine’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"rest","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" stub to refilling the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pool (and teaches it ","type":"text"},{"code":"meditate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), and adds ","type":"text"},{"code":"spell","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to the parser’s noise words,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so ","type":"text"},{"code":"cast the glow spell","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reaches ","type":"text"},{"code":"glow","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Its own lines are a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/Text","type":"reference"},{"text":", passed at init.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Casting runs gate, effect, pay. Availability is checked first; the effect runs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"second and may refuse on its own account with ","type":"text"},{"code":"require","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"reply","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; only an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"effect that finished pays. So a firebolt aimed at nothing costs no energy, and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"scroll read at the wrong wall survives.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"text":"Wiring it in","type":"heading","anchor":"Wiring-it-in"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import Gnusto","import GnustoSpellcasting","","extension Intent {","    #verb(\"glow\", [\"glow\"], [\"cast\", \"glow\"])","    #verb(","        \"firebolt\", [\"firebolt\"], [\"cast\", \"firebolt\"],","        [\"firebolt\", .directObject], [\"cast\", \"firebolt\", \"at\", .directObject])","}","","struct Tower: Game {","    let magic = Spellcasting(memorySlots: 3, maxMana: 12)","","    var content: GameContents { magic }","    var verbs: [SyntaxRule] { [.glow, .firebolt] }","","    var actions: [IntentAction] {","        magic.spell(.glow, cost: .cantrip) {","            say(\"Pale light seeps from your fingers.\")","        }","        magic.spell(.firebolt, cost: .energy(4)) {","            guard let target = command.directObject else {","                try reply(\"Cast firebolt at what?\")","            }","            target.vanish()","            say(\"Fire leaps from your hand and bursts against \\(target.definiteName).\")","        }","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost\/prepared(book:learnVia:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" spell carries its own memorize intent,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so the one ","type":"text"},{"code":"spell(_:called:cost:effect:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" call registers both halves:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["magic.spell(.unbar, cost: .prepared(book: spellbook, learnVia: .learnUnbar)) {","    try require(!wardedDoor.isOpen, else: \"The door already stands open.\")","    wardedDoor.isOpen = true","    say(\"The warding-marks gutter and die, and the door drifts open.\")","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Pass ","type":"text"},{"code":"book: nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the spell can be memorized anywhere; pass an item and it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has to be in hand.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"One memorize verb per prepared spell. ","type":"text"},{"code":"learnVia","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" registers a stage-4 action on that intent, and two spells declaring the same one collide: the bootstrap keeps the later and warns that it overrides the earlier. ","type":"text"},{"code":"memorize unbar","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"memorize seal","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are two intents, not one ","type":"text"},{"code":"memorize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with an object.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"text":"The worked example","type":"heading","anchor":"The-worked-example"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Sources\/Gramarye\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a small original game built to test the claim in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first sentence of this page. It runs one spell per paradigm and chains them so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each opens exactly one obstacle: the cantrip finds the scroll, the memorized","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"spell opens the warded door, the energy spell destroys the golem, the scroll","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"passes the wall. Remove any one of the four and the amulet is unreachable, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a stronger demonstration than four spells that happen to work. Its design","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"document is ","type":"text"},{"code":"docs\/games\/gramarye.md","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/gnustospellcasting"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://GnustoSpellcasting/documentation/GnustoSpellcasting/Spellcasting/spell(_:called:cost:effect:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"spell"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Intent","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto6IntentV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"called"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"cost"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"SpellCost","preciseIdentifier":"s:18GnustoSpellcasting9SpellCostO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"effect"},{"kind":"text","text":": () "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Void","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4Voida"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"IntentAction","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto12IntentActionV"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnustospellcasting\/spellcasting\/spell(_:called:cost:effect:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Registers one spell: the stage-4 behavior that casting its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"intent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"performs, and — for a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost\/prepared(book:learnVia:)"},{"type":"text","text":" spell — the behavior"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of memorizing it via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"prepareIntent"},{"type":"text","text":". Splice the result into the game’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"actions"},{"type":"text","text":" block."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/spell(_:called:cost:effect:)","title":"spell(_:called:cost:effect:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://GnustoSpellcasting/documentation/GnustoSpellcasting/Spellcasting/maxMana":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"maxMana","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxMana","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The full magical-energy pool ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rest"},{"text":" restores to.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/maxMana","url":"\/documentation\/gnustospellcasting\/spellcasting\/maxmana","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GnustoSpellcasting/documentation/GnustoSpellcasting/SpellCost":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"SpellCost","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SpellCost","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How a spell becomes available to cast, and what casting it costs — the axis"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that lets one spellcasting system express the common RPG magic paradigms"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"without changing how a spell’s "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"effect"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" is written.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost","url":"\/documentation\/gnustospellcasting\/spellcost","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SpellCost"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://GnustoSpellcasting/documentation/GnustoSpellcasting/Spellcasting/Text":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnustospellcasting\/spellcasting\/text","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Text","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/Text","abstract":[{"text":"The system’s own voice — every line the mechanics print, from the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"refusals at the availability gate to the ","type":"text"},{"code":"spells","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" report. A spell’s","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"effect"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" is the game’s prose and never passes through here. Override","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lines at init to re-skin.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Text","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"Spellcasting.Text"},"doc://GnustoSpellcasting/documentation/GnustoSpellcasting/SpellCost/energy(_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnustospellcasting\/spellcost\/energy(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"energy"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost\/energy(_:)","abstract":[{"text":"Draws the given amount from the shared magical-energy pool; refused when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the pool is too low. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rest"},{"text":" restores the pool to full. The amount must","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not be negative — that would pay the caster back and could refill the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pool past ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxMana"},{"text":" — and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Spellcasting.spell(_:called:cost:effect:)"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"rejects one with a "},{"type":"codeVoi